From 59067651ec71e074be62efc389af62ed663d8f71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:57:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 048/137] Input: qcom-spmi-haptics: Add the PM8350B (HAP520)
 haptics

HAP520, the haptics module of the PM8350B, is programmed like HAP530_HV
for DIRECT_PLAY and FIFO plays, with these differences (taken from the
downstream qcom-hv-haptics driver, which handles HAP_CFG/HAP_PTN
revision 2, what a PM8350B reports):

 - the FIFO is a fixed 640 samples: no MMAP_FIFO partitioning and no
   MEM_OP_ACCESS flush; toggling HAPTICS_EN gives a FIFO play a clean
   start instead;
 - the FIFO-empty threshold counts in steps of 40 samples (280 is used);
 - every FIFO write must be a 4-byte FIFO_DIN burst: a 1-byte write
   that meets the hardware reading the FIFO makes it drop three of every
   four samples, so the end of an effect is padded with silence;
 - TLRA_OL is counted by the RC clock, which is auto-calibrated: a
   period is programmed as 1.024 times its length;
 - the module is powered by its own boost (HAP_HBST), which follows it
   in hardware: Vmax is limited to 5 V when the boost is clamped, and a
   play waits (up to 20 ms) for the boost to be idle after the previous
   one;
 - the auto-resonance settings of HAP530 (duty cycles, zero-cross
   window, RAMP_DN_CFG2) do not apply; the hardware defaults are kept,
   as downstream does;
 - FAULT_CLR has no ZX_TO bit.

Boot firmware or a previous OS may leave the SoundWire pattern input
enabled (the downstream audio stack plays haptics as PCM from the LPASS
RX macro), the FIFO sample format other than two's complement, the drive
not waiting for the boost (FORCE_VREG_RDY) and the module enabled: set
all of them at probe.

Move the HAP530 specifics behind a variant description, selected by
compatible.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/input/misc/Kconfig             |   7 +-
 drivers/input/misc/qcom-spmi-haptics.c | 294 ++++++++++++++++++++++---
